ntos. El contrato [1], de 14.982,68 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos cerca del límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a factores como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No se puede asumir que haya abusos sin comprobar con más datos.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos junto al límite se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 47 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 9.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.3 to 7.7. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 14,982.68 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. These could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if multiple contracts served the same purpose. Review awardee A's contracts to ensure no single supplier was overused for similar needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["ubhlhSdPIBFxseVhcqrkhw%3D%3D","EC%2BDkC1UghE%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","ny45fu%2FFxnNSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}